  "interpretation": "The zero-register encoder is faster and its final visual tokens are less aligned with CLS, less mutually similar within an image, and slightly higher in centered energy. Those changes show that separate global and visual parameter paths absorb part of the routing role normally assigned to registers. However, the seven-register control is better at final semantic aggregation: it leads by 0.76 percentage points in peak online accuracy, 0.92 points in final online accuracy, 1.30 points in frozen CLS-centroid accuracy, and 0.68 points in frozen patch-mean centroid accuracy. The candidate's strongest semantic advantage occurs in blocks 6 through 9, peaking at block 7, but disappears by block 12. Registers therefore remain beneficial for top-layer semantic quality even after pathway specialization.",
